 ## Operating characteristics
@@ -128,8 +117,8 @@
 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N^3)$ to store the 3D texture/grid [G].
 *   **Performance:** Measured on standard meshes like the Stanford Bunny (35,947 vertices, 69,451 triangles) and automobile parts (156,229 vertices, 312,458 triangles) [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Provides exact Euclidean distances to the mesh surface, enabling high-quality rendering and isosurfacing. Handles complex geometry directly [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Computationally intensive for large meshes. Sensitive to mesh quality (holes, normals). Boundary handling requires careful tuning of `textureShell` [S1][S3, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** When exact distance to a scanned mesh is required for raymarching or implicit surface reconstruction.
-*   **When not to use:** For real-time applications with very high triangle counts where approximate methods are preferred, or when the mesh is not closed and topological containment is ambiguous.
